2003 in British Columbia, Canada. Sybil was born on November 15, 1940, in St. James, Jamaica to Lillian Wright and Josiah Wright (deceased).\\n\\nAIKMAN. BIRTHS - At Friendship Park Villa, in Liguanea, St. \",\"document\",[]],[\"s2855\",\"d1\",353,703,\"Andrews, Island of Jamaica, on the 22d October, the lady of Alexander AIKMAN, jun., Esq., printer to his Majesty, and to the Hon. House of Assembly, of a son. (The Edinburgh Advertiser of 10 January 1827)\\n\\nALLISON, Ovetta - Died at Brampton Civic Hospital on Thursday, January 10, 2013. She will be missed by Ian Allison, father of her two children. \",\"document\",[]],[\"s2856\",\"d1\",703,1053,\"She was a loving mother to Ianthe Allison and grandmother to Mercedes, Katrinna, Savannah and Shadrach. Another daughter, Yolande Allison, preceded Ovetta. She also precedes siblings, Edelmera Harrison, Getseta Thompson, Seymour (Chappo) O'Meally and Gloria Nelson. In Jamaica, Ovetta worked as Postmistress at both the Hayes and Alley post offices. \",\"document\",[]],[\"s2857\",\"d1\",1053,1451,\"She migrated to Canada in 1971 and worked at Bell Canada for 26 years until her retirement. A funeral service was held in the Ward Chapel, 52 Main Street South, Brampton on Saturday, January 19th. Cremation.\\n\\nPublished in the Toronto Star on January 12, 2013\\n\\nALLPORT, Mr. Arthur Reginald. Mother Charlotte Fischer b. Germany Father Walter Harrison Allport b. England. Spouse Bertha Mary Campbell. \",\"document\",[]],[\"s2858\",\"d1\",1451,1850,\"Born 23rd Dec. 1880, Jamaica, WI. Died North Vancouver, British Columbia, Canada, 2nd Oct. 1965, Residence West Vancouver, age 84.\\n\\nReference British Columbia Vital Records (BCVR) 1965 Death Registration #65-09-013305 Family History Library Film #2033798.\\n\\nALLWOOD, Mr. Frank Harold, born 1st July 1889 Jamaica, WI. Mother ? b. Jamaica, WI. Father James Allwood b. Jamaica, WI. Spouse Eileen Barry. \",\"document\",[]],[\"s3340\",\"d2\",0,278,\"---\\ntitle: Valicha by Miguel A. Hurtado, Jacksonville University Choral Union, Julian Bryson, Director\\ndate: 2025-04-26\\n---\\nCreative Arts Series\\n\\nCreative Arts SeriesThis Month\\n\\nJacksonville University Choirs Farewell Concert\\n\\nThursday, April 24 at 7:30 PM\\n\\nTERRY CONCERT HALL\\n\\n\",\"document\",[]],[\"s3341\",\"d2\",278,577,\"The Jacksonville University Choirs partner with the School of Art & Design to share an evening of music inspired by visual art. Part of CONNECT! a choral season of collaboration.\\n\\nHighlighted Event\\n\\nThursday, April 24 and Friday, April 25 at 7:30 PM\\n\\nSaturday, April 26 at 2:00 PM\\n\\nSWISHER THEATER\\n\\n\",\"document\",[]],[\"s3342\",\"d2\",577,963,\"For this series of performances, Jacksonville University Dance will push the boundaries of contemporary choreography with original works produced by our senior class. Join us for a concert of cutting-edge choreography and electrifying dance not to be missed, as we celebrate the Jacksonville University Dance graduating class of 2025.\\n\\nView the Creative Current Magazine of 2023-2024.\\n\\n\",\"document\",[]],[\"s3343\",\"d2\",963,1281,\"View the complete Creative Arts Series of 2024-2025.\\n\\nSPRING 2025 EVENTS\\n\\nSaturday, January 11 at 7:30 PM\\n\\nTERRY CONCERT HALL\\n\\nOur upcoming Ritz Chamber Players 2024-2025 season, themed \\\"Lift Every Voice,\\\" showcases the brilliance of Black composers from around the globe, offering a diverse and inspiring repertoire. \",\"document\",[]],[\"s3344\",\"d2\",1281,1659,\"We envision a collaboration where seniors involved with City of Jacksonville Senior Services could attend special performances at Terry Concert Hall on the campus of Jacksonville University on Fridays, prior to our regularly scheduled Ritz Chamber Players Saturday concerts. We look forward to discussing the ideal start time that works best for you and the seniors you serve.\\n\\n\",\"document\",[]],[\"s3418\",\"d3\",0,214,\"---\\ntitle: Chronology\\ndate: 2023-01-17\\n---\\nWelcome to our Midway Island Chronology page, a comprehensive online resource dedicated to unfolding the rich sequence of events that have shaped Midway Island's history. \",\"document\",[]],[\"s3419\",\"d3\",214,454,\"From its discovery in the 19th century to its pivotal role in World War II and its current status as a wildlife refuge, our Chronology offers a detailed and engaging timeline of this small yet significant atoll in the North Pacific Ocean.\\n\\n\",\"document\",[]],[\"s3420\",\"d3\",454,853,\"Perfect for historians, educators, students, or anyone fascinated by the intersection of nature and history, our Midway Island Chronology page is a gateway to understanding the enduring legacy of this remarkable island.\\n\\nChronology of Events for Midway Island\\n\\n►July 5, 1859, Tuesday – Captain N.C. Brooks of the Hawaiian Bark Gambia discovers the Island. Islands were named \\\"Middlebrook Islands\\\".\\n\\n\",\"document\",[]],[\"s3421\",\"d3\",853,1205,\"►August 28, 1867, Wednesday – Captain William Reynolds of the USS Lackawanna takes possession of the Island for the United States. Midway becomes the first offshore islands annexed by the U.S. government.\\n\\n►January 28, 1869, Thursday – The Navy adopts the name Midway Islands, according to a report submitted to the Senate Committee on Naval Affairs.\\n\\n\",\"document\",[]],[\"s3422\",\"d3\",1205,1581,\"►November 16, 1886, Tuesday – The schooner General Siegel was shipwrecked at Midway during a storm.\\n\\n►February 3, 1888, Friday – The British bark Wandering Minstrel was shipwrecked in Wells Harbor, during a storm.\\n\\n►January 17, 1899, Tuesday – The USS Bennington took possession of Wake Island, with the intention of having it used as a cable station between Midway and Guam. \",\"document\",[]],[\"s3876\",\"d4\",0,368,\"---\\ntitle: Vocal Area Network Choir Auditions\\ndate: 2025-06-09\\n---\\nSend new ads and updates to existing ads via\\n\\ne-mail to the .\\n\\nCurious about how we prefer to format bits of information on the Vocal Area Network website? See our VAN Style Guide.\\n\\nEditor's note: Vocal Area Network compiles and gently edits these ads for the benefit of the vocal ensemble community. \",\"document\",[]],[\"s3877\",\"d4\",368,743,\"Opinions expressed or claims made in these ads are the responsibility of the groups that post them.\\n\\nColor key for age of audition ads (green=fresh;\\n\\nred=old):\\n\\nless than 1 month old less than 3 months old more than 6 months old more than 12 months old\\n\\nbetween 3 and 6 months old\\n\\nless than 1 month old less than 3 months old more than 6 months old more than 12 months old\\n\\n\",\"document\",[]],[\"s3878\",\"d4\",743,1139,\"between 3 and 6 months old\\n\\nMusic on the Hill Festival ChorusMusic on the Hill Festival Chorus\\n\\n6/9/2025 2:56:25 PM\\n\\n(updated\\n\\n6/9/2025)\\n\\nVAN\\n\\nChoir Directory listing\\n\\n*** Rehearsals: Tuesday, Thursday *** Rehearsal neighborhood: Rowayton, CT\\n\\nMusic on the Hill invites experienced adult and teen choral singers to join the 22nd Annual Summer Chorus: \\\"Sing Evermore: Songs through Dark & Light.\\\" \",\"document\",[]]],\"required_scope\":{\"entity_scope\":\"learning institution matching all criteria\",\"time_scope\":\"as of 2023\"},\"rules_completion_required\":false,\"supported_task_outputs\":{},\"source_documents\":{\"d1\":{\"doc_id\":\"50603\",\"time_metadata\":{}},\"d2\":{\"doc_id\":\"12193\",\"time_metadata\":{}},\"d3\":{\"doc_id\":\"44033\",\"time_metadata\":{}},\"d4\":{\"doc_id\":\"12643\",\"time_metadata\":{}}},\"source_span_columns\":[\"id\",\"doc_id\",\"start\",\"end\",\"text\",\"source_role\",\"source_message_indices\"]}"}], "logical_call_index": 8, "response_format": "plain", "input_tokens_local": 7063, "output_token_reserve": 4096, "input_margin": 256, "max_model_len": 120000, "tokenization_request_sha256": "38dff2cc5fee66f6b68b55b976a3a9c28f8fa57f3b623c96875b1013933526e3", "tokenization_endpoint_sha256": "0ed12ee94b55bfdbc62fb247243af